    {
     "author": {
      "accountId": "557058:e25d94d0-bd50-4c2c-906c-14cdf85801fb",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/f53ee0691ccb59ede3ec232c18af4e16?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FCW-5.png",
       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/f53ee0691ccb59ede3ec232c18af4e16?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FCW-5.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/f53ee0691ccb59ede3ec232c18af4e16?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FCW-5.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/f53ee0691ccb59ede3ec232c18af4e16?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FCW-5.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Chris Wilper",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=557058%3Ae25d94d0-bd50-4c2c-906c-14cdf85801fb",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>Committed to trunk.  Fedora's logging is now all done consistently through slf4j APIs, and the legacy bridges are employed in order to get <b>all</b> log messages of libraries we depend on going through slf4j.</p>\n\n<p>Logback is used as the runtime logging implementation.  For the Fedora server, configuration is similar to that of log4j: The logback.xml file stored in $FEDORA_HOME/server/config can be modified to change log levels and filter by package + class in a variety of ways.  The default configuration is set to notice configuration changes while the server is running (\n    <span class=\"jira-issue-macro resolved\" data-jira-key=\"FCREPO-639\" >\n                <a href=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/browse/FCREPO-639\" class=\"jira-issue-macro-key issue-link\"  title=\"Allow log re-configuration without restart\" >\n            <img class=\"icon\" src=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/universal_avatar/view/type/issuetype/avatar/10315?size=medium\" />\n            FCREPO-639\n        </a>\n                                                    <span class=\"aui-lozenge aui-lozenge-subtle aui-lozenge-success jira-macro-single-issue-export-pdf\">Closed</span>\n            </span>\n).</p>\n\n<p>Client and server scripts (with the exception of fedora-rebuild.sh) use a default configuration logs only WARN or ERROR messages to the console, and ignores all others.  These can now be easily changed by modifying server/bin/logback.xml or client/bin/logback.xml.  As before, the rebuilder still uses the same logging configuration as the server, but sends its output to server/logs/fedora-rebuild.log by default.</p>\n\n<p>The fop, saxon, and imagemanip webapps are configured by default to send all WARN and ERROR messages to standard output which, for tomcat, means their errors will be logged in catalina.out by default.  This can be changed by modifying their respective WEB-INF/classes/logback.xml files.</p>\n\n<p>During development, when unit or integration tests are run, logging is by default configured to report INFO, WARN, and ERROR messages to STDOUT.  This can be changed by either modifying src/test/resources/logback.xml, or creating a non-version-controlled logback-test.xml file in the same directory.</p>",
